    "summary": "The complete candidate adds S2-03b activity-driven audit settings snapshots to the inherited settings, sender, saved Test and capture stack. The audit-logs owner retains bounded enabled/revision metadata, schedules reads after trusted activity, drops current unknown/disabled/expired events, and binds only future events to a fresh saved revision. Hosted app composition shares one AuditLog and snapshot owner across MCP and web and closes snapshots before storage. Timed-out native reads retain physical admission until settlement; late loads cannot restore evicted or closed state. The default downstream still discards; current-store dispatch, queues and retries remain S2-03c. System diagnostics remain separate. No package, schema, paid resource, MFA, provider operation or deployment topology is added by this slice; inherited complete-main architecture and policy impacts remain. The logging object CR remains applied: concrete SystemLogger uses distinct console/OTel SystemLogSink roles, with unchanged preparation and output behavior. DestinationSettingsService requires its sender; app composition supplies the real sender and tests use explicit roles. This restack preserves the original snapshot behavior and all prior PR238 inclusion.",
